	(text "ADS124S08: SPI mode 1, AVDD 5 V, logic 3.3 V. AIN0-3 read channels 1-4 against AINCOM = ground with the internal 2.5 V reference and the PGA bypassed (a ground-referenced input is outside the PGA range)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 21 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b8f5db63-9516-5cd4-b569-69ad88314e0b")
	)
	(text "Both release their data output when CS is high (DAC60508 section 8.5, ADS124S08 section 9.5.1), so they share SPI_MISO without a buffer."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 33 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c7bc2b76-9bd3-51a2-9116-1a4dcbc8536a")
	)
	(text "DAC60508Z: 12-bit, outputs at zero after reset. On 3.3 V its 2.5 V reference needs the divider on with gain 2 (GAIN register), giving 0-2.5 V; until firmware writes that, the reference alarm holds every output at 0 V. SDI is latched on falling SCLK edges (SPI mode 1)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 15 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f399133b-6a1b-5c38-aad2-054e1d62650e")
	)
